- Affected component: BGP export on router1 (FRR bgpd) is not advertising the LAN 195.11.14.0/24 toward its eBGP neighbor.
- Mechanism: Router1 has a BGP-learned route to 200.1.1.0/24 via router2, so pc1’s probes are forwarded to pc2. However, router2 has no route to 195.11.14.0/24, so pc2’s replies cannot return; from pc1 this appears as timeouts. When pc2 pings 195.11.14.x, its default gateway (router2 at 200.1.1.1) immediately generates “Destination Net Unreachable” because it lacks any route to 195.11.14.0/24.
