is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: router1
diagnosis_text:
- Affected component: BGP export on router1 (FRR bgpd) is not advertising the LAN 195.11.14.0/24 toward its eBGP neighbor.
- Mechanism: Router1 has a BGP-learned route to 200.1.1.0/24 via router2, so pc1’s probes are forwarded to pc2. However, router2 has no route to 195.11.14.0/24, so pc2’s replies cannot return; from pc1 this appears as timeouts. When pc2 pings 195.11.14.x, its default gateway (router2 at 200.1.1.1) immediately generates “Destination Net Unreachable” because it lacks any route to 195.11.14.0/24.
- Localization: 
  - router1 (eth1 195.11.14.1/24; eBGP over eth0 193.10.11.1) — FRR config has no “network 195.11.14.0/24” (show running-config confirms only neighbor, no network/redistribute).
  - router2 (eth1 200.1.1.1/24) — routing table has only connected 200.1.1.0/24 and 193.10.11.0/24 with no BGP route to 195.11.14.0/24, matching its ICMP unreachable behavior.
- Root cause: router1 is not originating/advertising 195.11.14.0/24 into BGP, so router2 never learns a route to pc1’s subnet.
- Corrective fix: On router1, configure BGP to announce the LAN:
  router bgp 1
   address-family ipv4 unicast
    network 195.11.14.0/24
  or use “redistribute connected” with appropriate policy. After commit, verify router2 installs BGP route to 195.11.14.0/24 and end-to-end pings succeed both ways.

=== END ===